* tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v10_sim_ready.spice -- auto-generated by
* script/gen_chip_sim_ready_v10.py, from:
*   /sessions/dreamy-ecstatic-heisenberg/mnt/TR-1um_Async_I2C/schematic/tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v10_lvs.spice
* (the LVS-confirmed-clean V10 chip netlist, RING_OSC excluded -- see
* this script's own module docstring for why the source file already
* excludes RING_OSC with no manual stripping needed). Mechanical
* fixes applied on top of the verbatim source, all required for a
* real ngspice run (none change electrical intent) -- same fix classes
* as V9's gen_chip_sim_ready_v9.py, whose docstring has the full
* diagnosis/rationale for each:
*   1) all 378 bare M-line transistor instances -> X-line
*      (subckt-call) form, so ip62_models' PMOS/NMOS .subckt wrappers
*      resolve them (KLayout's own bare-M LVS convention doesn't).
*   2) 37 bracket-vector net names (145
*      occurrences, e.g. tx_data[0] -> tx_data_0), everywhere they
*      appear.
*   3) 2 malformed comment-continuation line(s) in the
*      i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm PININFO block (bare "+" -> "*+") --
*      the real root cause of V9's own "too few nodes" ngspice error
*      on the x2 instantiation; see gen_chip_sim_ready_v9.py's
*      docstring fix #3 for the full diagnosis.
*   4) 4 diode instance parameter(s) renamed A=/P= ->
*      AREA=/PJ= (DD1/DD2 inside OSS_ESD_5V_DIO) -- ngspice's native
*      diode instance parser doesn't accept the short forms KLayout's
*      LVS writer emits; values unchanged, purely a keyword-spelling
*      fix.
*   5) 4 bare-M devices (originally model=NMOSE, all inside
*      the OSS_ESD_5V_* pad-ESD cells) renamed to model=MNE -- NMOSE is
*      a KLayout DRC/LVS device-recognition label with no SPICE-library
*      counterpart; MNE is ip62_models' extended-drain NMOS and what
*      these cells' own source xschem schematic actually specifies
*      (property model=MNE) -- see gen_chip_sim_ready_v9.py's docstring
*      for the full cross-check (same ESD cells, unchanged from v9).
*      This is the best-supported mapping found but IS an inference;
*      sanity-check ESD-cell nodes on first real run.
* DO NOT hand-edit -- regenerate instead.

** tr_1um_i2c_slave_async_v10_lvs.spice -- chip-level LVS reference netlist (V10,
** core+GIO only -- RING_OSC not yet integrated, see
** gen_lvs_spice_ringosc_v10.py for that).
** Generated by script/gen_lvs_spice_top_v10.py from:
**   1) schematic/i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm_v10.spice (core, LVS-clean per
**      design_notes.md 108.51 -- "V10コアセル単体LVSクリーン達成")
**   2) simulations/OSS_FRAME_GIO.spice (GIO pad-ring frame, transistor
**      level, unchanged from V9 -- same physical frame)
**   3) schematic/gio_connections.json (base GIO<->core connection map,
**      derived + cross-verified design_notes.md 78.1/78.4 for V9) with
**      the 20 signal-net terminals OVERRIDDEN from
**      schematic/v10_signal_routing_plan.json's own per-net "terminal"
**      field (V10's pad-pairing-aware reassignment, design_notes.md
**      108.57) -- see this script's own module docstring for exactly
**      which terminals differ from V9's assignment and why the rest of
**      the 43-terminal map is safely reused verbatim.
** x1 = OSS_FRAME_GIO, x2 = i2c_slave_async_nrow_fm. Nets prefixed NC_
** are genuinely unconnected on both sides -- each gets its own unique
** floating net name so LVS sees them as independently floating,
** matching the real chip.
** Top subckt declares its 16 real bond-pad ports explicitly (P1-P7,
** VSS, P9-P15, VDD -- P8 does not exist in this frame), matching v9's
** own top-level-pin fix (design_notes.md 79.13).

